The '''Imperial office complex''',<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman AD">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> also known as the '''IOC building''',<ref name="WAY?">{{Andor|Who Are You?}}</ref> was a building located partially in the [[Palmo Plaza|main plaza]] of [[Palmo]], the [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]]. In [[3 BBY]] it included the [[Bureau of Standards Ghorman field office]]<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> a department of the [[Imperial Bureau of Standards]] tasked with the standardization of [[ghorlectipod]]-related inventories and audits.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|bureau-of-standards-ghorman-field-office|Bureau of Standards Ghorman field office}}</ref> When [[Imperial Security Bureau|ISB]] [[supervisor]] [[Dedra Meero]] was given control of Ghorman, she used the building as a staging ground facilitating the [[Ghorman project|Ghorman Project.]]<ref name="WAY?" /> 

==Description==
The Imperial office complex was a building located at [[Palmo Plaza]]<ref name="WAY?" /> in [[Palmo]], the [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]]. It included a number of offices including the [[Bureau of Standards Ghorman field office]] as well as an [[Imperial Security Bureau]] [[Imperial Security Bureau safe room|safe room]].<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> 

==History==
In [[3 BBY]], [[Syril Karn]] worked as the [[Division Chief]] for the [[Imperial Bureau of Standards]] field office while really working undercover for the Imperial Security Bureau to foment the [[Ghorman Front]], a local rebel cell. After being contacted by the Front, Karn attempted to gain entry to the complex after hours but did not have the after-hours clearance. However he was able to persuade the [[Unidentified Imperial office complex guard 1|two]] [[Unidentified Imperial office complex guard 2|guards]] to let him by telling them he needed his notes from his office to prepare for a presentation with the [[Sector Committee]] tomorrow. After grabbing a [[datapad]] from his office, Karn when to the Imperial Security Bureau safe room within the building to update [[Dedra Meero]], his lover and [[ISB Supervisor]], about the contact.<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> At least a [[Standard week|week]] later, the ISB conducted a security search of the Bureau of Standards field office in which they found a [[listening device]] in Karn's office planted by the Ghorman Front.<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The office complext appeared in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', first appearing in the series's fourth episode, "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]," which was released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> It is identified in the episode as "the Imperial office complex" by the [[Wikipedia:English language|English language]] audio descriptions.<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman AD">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> The [[Databank (2014-)|Star Wars Databank]] entry for the Imperial Security Bureau safe room characterizes it as "an unassuming Imperial office building".<ref name="Safe room databank">{{Databank|imperial-security-bureau-safe-room|Imperial Security Bureau safe room}}</ref>

